Finance Data Dictionary Interactive Portal (HTML + AI Enabled) - Business Requirements & Functional Specification
Executive Summary
Create a centralized Finance Data Dictionary Portal hosted entirely on a shared drive. The solution will provide chartfield education, combination validation, terminology lookup, tree exploration and future AI capabilities.
Project Objectives
Provide a single source of truth, reduce dependency on Excel, enable self-service validation and support future AI guidance.
Scope
•	ChartFields Overview
•	Combination Validator
•	Finance Terminology
•	ChartField Trees Explorer
•	Miscellaneous Knowledge Area
•	AI Assistant Integration
Critical Design Principles
•	Reference Excel workbook is sample/reference only.
•	All solution artifacts remain on shared drive.
•	No external database required.
•	JSON configuration drives application logic.
•	Local rule engine first, AI second.
Reference Workbook Usage
•	Workbook provides sample values, definitions and structures only.
•	Portal must continue functioning without workbook availability.
Tab 1 – ChartFields Overview
•	Visual poster-style representation of Business Unit, Function, Business Line, Market, Account, Alternate Account, Affiliate, Project ID and Book Code.
•	Hover and click interactions for definitions and examples.
Tab 2 – Combination Validator
•	Nine chartfield input controls available.
•	Fields are optional and not mandatory.
•	Validate only rules applicable to entered fields.
•	Return Valid, Invalid or No Applicable Rule Found.
•	Display violated rule, explanation and recommendation.
Validation Engine
•	Store rules in JSON.
•	Support active Combination Edit logic.
•	Evaluate ACT_PROJ, ACT_AFF, BL_PRJ, MKT_FCT, BK_ACT and other active rules.
AI Integration Rules
•	No AI invocation during standard validation.
•	AI only for Explain Result, recommendations, free-form questions or unmatched cases.
•	Use Local JSON => Rule Engine => AI escalation model.
Tab 3 – Finance Terminology
•	Searchable glossary using terminology definitions.
•	Display definition, examples, source systems and consuming systems.
Tab 4 – ChartField Trees
•	Collapsible hierarchy browser.
•	Search nodes and tree metadata.
Tab 5 – Miscellaneous
•	Asset Classes
•	Employee Definitions
•	Employee Measures
•	TimeSpans
•	Project Types
Shared Drive Architecture
•	Store HTML, CSS, JS, JSON, images and reference workbook on shared drive only.
•	No storage outside shared drive.
Security Requirements
•	API keys must never be stored in client-side code.
•	JWT tokens must not be exposed in browser.
•	Use backend proxy for future AI integration.
Future Enhancements
•	Admin page for JSON refresh.
•	Workbook-to-JSON conversion utility.
•	Advanced AI assistant.
Acceptance Criteria
•	Portal loads within three seconds.
•	Users can validate chartfield combinations.
•	Users can search terminology.
•	AI is called only when required.





















